# qkt Bybit project

This project was generated by `qkt create template --kind bybit`.

It starts a QKT daemon wired directly to Bybit REST. There is no gateway service.
Testnet is enabled by default.

## First Run

```bash
cp .env.example .env
$EDITOR .env
docker compose --env-file .env config --quiet
make up
make status
```

## Environment Values

Required to trade through Bybit:

- `QKT_IMAGE_TAG`: QKT image tag. The generated default pins to the QKT version
  that created this project.
- `BYBIT_API_KEY`, `BYBIT_API_SECRET`: Bybit API credentials.

Usually keep defaults:

- `BYBIT_TESTNET`: `true` uses Bybit testnet. Set to `false` only for real
  money.

Optional:

- `TELEGRAM_ENABLED`, `TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN`, `TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID`: alerts.

Keep `.env` out of Git.

## Commands

- `make up`: start the QKT daemon.
- `make down`: stop containers without deleting state.
- `make restart`: restart QKT.
- `make logs`: tail daemon logs.
- `make status` / `make list`: show deployed strategies.
- `make deploy STRAT=<name>`: deploy `/strategies/<name>.qkt` as `<name>`.
- `make resync-dry-run STRAT=<name>`: validate replacement without changing the running strategy.
- `make resync STRAT=<name>`: replace only that running deployment.
- `make reconcile STRAT=<name>`: compare QKT ledger to broker/account state.
- `make stop STRAT=<name>`: stop one deployment.

## Strategy Flow

1. Use testnet credentials first.
2. Review and backtest the strategy outside this deployment repo.
3. Copy the live-ready `.qkt` file into `strategies/`.
4. Deploy with `make deploy STRAT=<name>`.
5. For edits, run `make resync-dry-run`, then `make resync`, then `make reconcile`.

